MACRO:
  ☐ Require direct tick await
  ✔ Ban shadowing of hardware parameters
    - DONE: check_no_param_shadowing (all modes) — a `let` binding (incl. tuple
      patterns) that reuses a port name is a spanned compile error. Unit tests +
      ui/fail/param_shadowing.rs.
  ✔ Require only one top-level loop shape
    - DONE: check_single_top_level_loop (sequential-like) — exactly one top-level
      `loop`, and it must be the final statement (a second loop / trailing code is
      unreachable). "No loop at all" was already rejected. Unit tests +
      ui/fail/multiple_top_level_loops.rs.
  ☐ Warn on persistent state mutation before tick
  ✔ Check all combinational outputs are assigned on all paths
    - DONE: copper_analysis::check_definite_assignment, enforced in the macro's
      combinational arm (sequential Out HOLDS when unwritten = enabled register,
      so this applies to combinational modules only; see design doc item 2)
  ☐ Reject stateful constructs in combinational modules
    - Maybe allow stuff that can be unrolled into combinational logic (e.g. for loops with constant bounds)

OTHER:
  ☐ IR-level dependency graph analysis to detect combinational loops  [DEFERRED to item 6]
    - reject combinational loops that dont pass through a register, memory latency, synchronizer, or other stateful primative
    - NOT an item-2 intra-CFG add: intra-module comb loops are unexpressible
      (Rust rejects the use-before-def); the real case is cross-module, needing
      item 6's inter-module producer->consumer wiring DAG. Runtime oscillation
      detection (executor OSCILLATION_THRESHOLD panic) covers it meanwhile.


================================================================================
TESTING — COMPREHENSIVE PLAN
================================================================================
Consolidated, prioritized test backlog (drafted 2026-08-03). Convention: ✔ = done
(file noted), ◐ = partial, ☐ = to write. "Equiv" = sim ≡ transpiled SystemVerilog
under Verilator via tests/common (the project correctness bar). "Oracle" = sim (or
transpiled SV) checked against an independent Rust reference. Verilator-dependent
tests are slower; oracle-only tests are pure `cargo test`.

Shared harness reference: tests/common/mod.rs (EquivalenceTest), fixture pattern
= tests/fixtures/*_dut.rs (`include!` for sim + `include_str!` for transpile).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
P0 — highest value / least effort (do first)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ✔ Randomized / property-based differential testing  [DONE 2026-08-03]
     ✔ Seeded PRNG helper (SplitMix64) in tests/common/mod.rs (`Rng`).
     ✔ Combinational random differential (sim vs Rust ref AND vs Verilator, 500/module):
       ripple_carry_adder, one_bit_comparator, rotate_right, gray_to_binary,
       priority_encode → tests/randomized_combinational_equivalence.rs
     ✔ Sequential random-stimulus differential (400/module): up_down_counter,
       accumulator_en, shift_register → tests/randomized_sequential_equivalence.rs
     ☐ FOLLOW-UPS still open:
        ☐ mux (array-input) — needs array-port support; untested anywhere
        ☐ lfsr / det_010 / traffic_light random streams (need FSM reference models)

  ✔ Tracked regression for the transpiler bit-width-inference GAP  [DONE 2026-08-03]
     ✔ `[Logic; N]` array-local + tuple-returning helper → assert transpile_source
       ERRORS with "cannot infer bit width" → copper-codegen/tests/transpile_inference_gaps.rs
       (expect_err flips loudly the day inference is fixed — see file header).

  ✔ Executor guardrail panics  [DONE 2026-08-03 → tests/executor_guardrails.rs]
     ✔ Module-completion panic: a module future returning Poll::Ready → panic.
     ✔ Multiple-driver behavior: PREVENTED at compile time (`Out` is !Clone);
       compile_fail doctest on `Out` (copper-core/src/port.rs). Contract = single writer.
     ◐ Untracked-output: behavior PINNED (stale-for-one-settle); the warning/error
       itself remains unimplemented (finding surfaced, see SIMULATOR section above).
     ✔ Combinational chain convergence / oscillation detection → tests/simulator_corner_cases.rs

