     [DEFERRED — it's a WARNING; trybuild asserts on errors, so needs a different
     test path (or promotion to an error). Design call pending.]
  ☐ Require direct tick await (reject aliased/wrapped `clk` tick)  [DEFERRED]

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
P2 — equivalence coverage per language construct (sim ≡ SV; fill the matrix)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Already covered: counter, up_down_counter, accumulator_en, slow_counter, lfsr,
  det_010, mac_fsm, mac_pipeline, traffic_light, shift_register, pattern_detector,
  priority_encode, rotate_right, one_bit_comparator, ripple_carry_adder, gray_to_binary.
  Construct SUPPORT probed empirically via the copper-transpile CLI (2026-08-03):
    SUPPORTED → equivalence-tested: wide datapaths, `*`, `-`/neg, `<<`/`>>`, `%`,
      `==`, statement `match`. UNSUPPORTED → pinned in
      copper-codegen/tests/unsupported_constructs.rs: array-typed ports, `/`,
      `arithmetic_shift_right` (and `lt_logic`/`zero_extend` methods, noted there).
      NOTE the `/` vs `%` asymmetry: `%` transpiles, `/` does not.
  ✔ Wide datapath (Bits<16>) + multiply + multi-output fan-in → ONE DUT covers all
     three: tests/wide_datapath_equivalence.rs (datapath16: sum/prod/diff, 500 random).
  ✔ Multiply datapath — covered by datapath16 (`*`).
  ✔ Multi-output combinational fan-in — covered by datapath16 (3 Out, shared reads).
  ◐ Nested match / enum FSM with >4 states → tests/fsm_six_state_equivalence.rs (seq6,
     6 enum states). Runs sim_only: sim≡reference PASSES, sim≡SV BLOCKED on the Moore-
     output-registered CODEGEN bug (see TRANSPILATION). Flip to full equiv when fixed.
  ☐ Array-typed ports: mux (`In<[Bits<W>; ELS]>`) — UNSUPPORTED, pinned as a gap
     (unsupported_constructs.rs::array_typed_port_is_unsupported); needs codegen work.
  ☐ Wide Bits<32>/Bits<64> specifically (datapath16 is 16-bit; 32/64 still untested).
  ☐ Signed arithmetic / arithmetic_shift_right — asr UNSUPPORTED, pinned as a gap.
  ☐ Divide / modulo datapath — `/` UNSUPPORTED (pinned); `%` supported but untested
     (a Verilator equiv needs a zero-divisor guard).
  ☐ Nested tick awaits (tick inside an inner loop/branch) — Verilator-checked timing
  ☐ RegOut Moore output (write-before-tick) equivalence, standalone (already covered
     indirectly by mac_fsm / sipo_block / pattern_detector_2 equivalence tests)

