P5 — Large integration (flagship examples, currently ZERO cargo-test coverage)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ✔ rv32i_cpu: 10 known programs (addi..bubblesort) run to halt, assert final a0.
     → tests/rv32i_integration.rs::scalar_cpu_matches_known_results.
  ✔ rv32i_cpu_pipelined: same 10 + the pipeline-specific ones (RAW forwarding=3,
     load-use stall=43, jal=7) → pipelined_cpu_matches_known_results; PLUS a direct
     scalar-vs-pipelined differential on the common programs → scalar_and_pipelined_agree.
     Structure: cfg(not(test)) on each example `fn main` + `include!` (scalar at crate
     root, pipelined in `mod pl` with its harness `pub`). CPUs don't transpile (Vec
     port + Memory + submodules), so this is a sim self-check, not a Verilator equiv.
     NOTE (found probing): the standalone transpiler PANICS on rv32i_cpu
     ("gate guarantees at least one tick", control_extract.rs:95) instead of a clean
     error — a codegen robustness bug, logged for later (needs sign-off to fix).
  ✔ uart/system: tx→rx loopback self-check → tests/uart_integration.rs.
     - uart_single_channel_loopback: 6 bytes (framing edges) round-trip tx→rx.
     - uart_dual_channel_no_crosstalk: two channels transmit different bytes on the
       same cycle; each arrives on its own channel (no cross-contamination).
     Same cfg(not(test))-main + top-level `include!` structure (self-contained file,
     so no `mod`/`pub` needed). Sim self-check, not a Verilator equiv.
  ☐ uart/rx standalone example — its own testbench not yet lifted (system.rs, which
     embeds tx+rx, is the integration path and IS covered above).

